{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtMoS1YoHWVbmYf3HrZK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a `codex-sandboxed` lane to `run.sh`. It runs the same `codex exec` as the `codex` lane under `sandbox/agent.sb`, the way `kimi` does. I ran it once on the fizz task and it exited 0. The details are in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Changes**\n- **`run.sh`**: new `codex_sandboxed_run` function and a `codex-sandboxed` case. Flags, prompt, `final.txt` output and timeout match the `codex` lane.\n- **`README.md`**: lists the new lane. I also corrected the note about Codex login. On this machine Codex logs in with `~/.codex/auth.json`, not `CODEX_API_KEY`.\n- **`sandbox/agent.sb`**: unchanged.\n- **`ANSWER.md`**: what I did, what I checked, and the caveats.\n\n**How the fence works**\n- Codex needs its login from `~/.codex/auth.json`, and the sandbox blocks the real home. So the lane gives Codex a scratch `CODEX_HOME` in `/tmp` with copies of `auth.json`, `config.toml` and `installation_id`.\n- The whole Codex process runs under the profile. The agent's shell is a child of it, so it inherits the same restrictions.\n- I checked the profile directly: reading `~/.codex/auth.json`, listing `~` and writing into `~` are all denied. Writing to `/tmp` works.\n\n**Test run**\n- `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed 1` exited 0 in 23 seconds. The agent found the bug (multiples of 15 hit the \"Fizz\" branch first), fixed its scratch copy, and confirmed `FizzBuzz`.\n- The repo's `tasks/fizz/fizz.py` is unchanged. Nothing is committed.\n\n**Caveats (details in ANSWER.md)**\n- The agent's shell can read the copied `auth.json` in `/tmp`. That is not the real home, but it is a credential the sandboxed agent can reach. Switching to a `CODEX_API_KEY` would remove the need to copy it.\n- The `auth.json` file was last modified on Nov 4, so a token refresh may happen during a run. A rotated refresh token could leave the real file stale. I did not check whether that happened.\n- The copied config lists MCP servers under the real home. They fail under the sandbox, and the errors are logged to `agent.err`. The run still completes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":40552,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":392},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0bf658d3-5a80-4699-8de4-798e2491bffa","uuid":"482062c8-2d37-4cec-bff6-2155c168ee94","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:13:01.749Z","request_id":"req_011CgtMoRrNraGw3dawK5PUM"}
